/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
| y+ on all wall patches.                                                    |
|                                                                             |
| Output: postProcessing/yPlus/0/yPlus.dat  (min/max/average per patch)      |
|         plus a yPlus volScalarField at each write time                      |
|                                                                             |
| This one matters for this case. The layer stack is sized for y+ ~ 2.5, and  |
| the wall functions chosen in 0.orig are only the right choice while y+      |
| stays in that range. Check this before trusting the forces - the campaign   |
| tooling records the wing and wheel averages for exactly that reason.        |
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

yPlus
{
    type            yPlus;
    libs            (fieldFunctionObjects);

    writeControl    writeTime;
    executeControl  writeTime;

    log             yes;
}


